CHUNK [119 bytes]: " to account for simultaneous agent generation.\n\n### Round 4: Concurrent Execution & UI Synchronization\n\n**1. How should"
CHUNK [125 bytes]: " the UI handle multiple simultaneous text streams?**\n*   **Recommendation:** Use **Parallel Response Cards** that appear side"
CHUNK [97 bytes]: "-by-side below the user's prompt, then \"collapse\" or \"commit\" into the main vertical history once"
CHUNK [124 bytes]: " finished.\n*   **Reasoning:** In a standard vertical chat, three agents streaming text simultaneously would cause the screen"
CHUNK [116 bytes]: " to jump violently. By placing them in horizontal columns or a grid during the \"Generating\" state, the user can scan"
CHUNK [122 bytes]: " all responses at once. Once all agents finish, the responses are appended to the permanent vertical transcript.\n\n**2. How"
CHUNK [125 bytes]: " should the system handle local hardware limits?**\n*   **Recommendation:** Implement a **Concurrency Queue**.\n*   **Reasoning"
CHUNK [112 bytes]: ":** If a user @mentions four agents using local Llama 3 models, most consumer GPUs will run out of VRAM or crawl"
CHUNK [120 bytes]: " to a halt trying to run four inference instances. The UI should show all four agents \"Thinking,\" but the backend should"
CHUNK [84 bytes]: " process them 1 or 2 at a time (if local) while processing API-based agents (OpenAI/"
