CHUNK [97 bytes]: "  \n**Focus:** Local-first, human-in-the-loop multi-agent orchestration.\n\n## 1. Problem Statement\n"
CHUNK [138 bytes]: "Managing multiple AI agents for complex projects is currently fragmented. Users have to switch between tools to manage RAG, model settings"
CHUNK [124 bytes]: ", and different personas. Existing multi-agent frameworks often lean toward \"autonomous\" behavior, which is hard to control,"
CHUNK [116 bytes]: " expensive, and prone to \"hallucination loops.\" \n\n**Orchestra** solves this by providing a unified environment where"
CHUNK [152 bytes]: " a human acts as the director, managing stateful conversations between specialized agents with full control over the narrative via \"Snapshotting\" and \"@"
CHUNK [87 bytes]: "mentions.\"\n\n## 2. Ideal User\n*   **Power Users & Researchers:** Who need to compare how"
CHUNK [107 bytes]: " different models/prompts handle the same data.\n*   **Developers:** Who want to test MCP tools and function"
CHUNK [102 bytes]: " calling in a controlled environment.\n*   **Writers/Creatives:** Who want to maintain \"world-building\""
CHUNK [119 bytes]: " state with different characters (agents) that have specific memories.\n\n## 3. Platform & Technical Stack\n*   **Platform"
CHUNK [122 bytes]: ":** Desktop Application (Electron or Tauri).\n*   **Reasoning:** Essential for local filesystem access (MCP servers), local"
CHUNK [101 bytes]: " model management (Hugging Face/GGUF), and low-latency RAG indexing.\n*   **Inference Engine:** Hybrid"
CHUNK [101 bytes]: ". Support for local providers (Ollama, LocalAI) and API providers (OpenAI, Anthropic).\n*   **Database"
CHUNK [110 bytes]: ":** SQLite for chat history, agent profiles, and room states.\n*   **Vector Store:** LanceDB or ChromaDB (local"
CHUNK [79 bytes]: "-first) for RAG and agent memories.\n\n## 4. Core User Experience (Step-by-Step)\n"
CHUNK [94 bytes]: "1.  **Agent Creation:** User defines an agent (e.g., \"Python Expert\"). They select a model (e."
CHUNK [82 bytes]: "g., GPT-4o or a local Llama-3), set temperature, write a system prompt, and toggle"
CHUNK [100 bytes]: " specific MCP tools from the library.\n2.  **Room Setup:** User creates a \"Project Room.\" They upload"
CHUNK [104 bytes]: " specific PDFs/Markdown files and set a \"Room Goal\" (Global System Prompt).\n3.  **The Orchestration Chat"
CHUNK [85 bytes]: ":**\n    *   The user types a message.\n    *   To get an AI response, the user must `@"
CHUNK [119 bytes]: "mention` an agent.\n    *   The mentioned agent processes the room context + RAG docs + full chat history and responds.\n"
CHUNK [111 bytes]: "    *   Other agents \"listen\" (the message is added to the stateful history) but do not respond until mentioned"
CHUNK [112 bytes]: ".\n4.  **Snapshotting:** At any point, the user clicks \"Snapshot.\" This saves the exact current state of the chat"
CHUNK [106 bytes]: ", agent memories, and room configuration.\n5.  **Forking:** The user can go back to an earlier Snapshot and"
CHUNK [114 bytes]: " \"Fork\" it, starting a new branch of the conversation without losing the original.\n\n## 5. Must-Have Features (MVP)"
CHUNK [120 bytes]: "\n*   **Agent Persona Engine:** Detailed control over system prompts, individual agent memories, and LLM parameters.\n*   "
CHUNK [110 bytes]: "**Centralized Tool Library:** An interface to manage MCP servers. Users can enable/disable tools (e.g., Google"
CHUNK [99 bytes]: " Search, Filesystem Read, SQL Executor) per agent.\n*   **Stateful Rooms:** Rooms that store history"
CHUNK [115 bytes]: " and RAG context locally; no need to resend full context windows manually.\n*   **Strict Manual Triggering:** Agents"
CHUNK [120 bytes]: " only respond when @mentioned or when a \"Continue\" button is pressed.\n*   **Model Flexibility:** Support for downloading"
CHUNK [97 bytes]: " GGUF models from Hugging Face or uploading local model files.\n*   **Snapshot & Fork:** A version"
CHUNK [97 bytes]: "-control-like system for chat states.\n*   **RAG Integration:** Local PDF/Text ingestion with text"
CHUNK [104 bytes]: " embedding support.\n\n## 6. Data Persistence & Access Control\n*   **User Accounts:** None required (Local"
CHUNK [107 bytes]: "-only application).\n*   **Access Control:** Local filesystem permissions.\n*   **Data Entities:**\n    *   **"
CHUNK [97 bytes]: "Agents:** Name, Model ID, System Prompt, Parameter Set, Memory Vector ID.\n    *   **Rooms:** Goal"
CHUNK [101 bytes]: ", System Prompt, Document Index, Participant List.\n    *   **Snapshots:** UUID, Timestamp, Room State"
CHUNK [101 bytes]: " Blob, Message History.\n    *   **Tools:** MCP Server URL/Path, Tool Schema, Permission Status.\n\n## 7"
CHUNK [117 bytes]: ". Technical Requirements\n*   **MCP Support:** Ability to connect to local or remote Model Context Protocol servers.\n*"
CHUNK [119 bytes]: "   **A2A/WebSocket:** Internal messaging bus to allow the UI to communicate with the local inference engine and the MCP"
CHUNK [117 bytes]: " servers.\n*   **Reasoning/Tool Use:** The orchestration layer must support JSON-mode or Function Calling to interpret"
CHUNK [112 bytes]: " when an agent wants to use an MCP tool.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of MVP Constraints\n*   **No Autonomous Loops:** Saves"
CHUNK [114 bytes]: " on costs and increases reliability.\n*   **Local First:** Protects privacy and allows for heavy model management.\n"
CHUNK [106 bytes]: "*   **Human-Centric:** The user is always the final arbiter of which agent speaks next.\n\n**Next Steps:**\n1"
CHUNK [92 bytes]: ".  Finalize the UI/UX wireframes for the \"History Tree\" (Snapshots).\n2.  Define the specific"
CHUNK [98 bytes]: " MCP servers to be included in the \"Standard Library\" (e.g., Fetch, Google Search, Local File Read"
CHUNK [59 bytes]: ").\n3.  Select the local embedding model for the RAG engine."
--- STREAM EOF ---

